    "normalization": "NFD accent stripping and casefold used only for retrieval labels; raw source text retained unchanged",
    "classified_leads": [
      {
        "printed_page": 565,
        "sentence_index": 25,
        "raw": "Page_Divider_Tag The Bhīls of the Pusad Taluqa of the Basim district , or at least some of them , speak a dialect which is almost identical with Kōlāmī .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 565,
        "sentence_index": 26,
        "raw": "The number of speakers of Bhīlī in Basim has been estimated at 375 .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 565,
        "sentence_index": 27,
        "raw": "We do not , however , know whether all of them speak the same dialect , and the Basim figures have , therefore , been added to the total for other",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 566,
        "sentence_index": 2,
        "raw": "Bhīl dialects .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 566,
        "sentence_index": 3,
        "raw": "The specimen of Bhīlī received from Basim , on the other hand , must be dealt with in this place .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 566,
        "sentence_index": 4,
        "raw": "In most respects it agrees with the specimen of Kōlāmī printed above .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 566,
        "sentence_index": 11,
        "raw": "These forms throw light on Kōlāmī amd , which must be derived from avnd .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 566,
        "sentence_index": 17,
        "raw": "On the whole , they are the same as in Kōlāmī .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 566,
        "sentence_index": 19,
        "raw": "The numerals are the same as in Kōlāmī .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 566,
        "sentence_index": 22,
        "raw": "From this fact we must infer that the genders in Kōlāmī are distinguished in the same way as in Telegu .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 566,
        "sentence_index": 25,
        "raw": "In ordinary Kōlāmī such forms are commonly used in all connexions .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 566,
        "sentence_index": 26,
        "raw": "In Bhīlī we find forms such as innen bālā , thy son , where the possessive pronoun agrees with the qualified noun in the same way as in Gōṇḍī .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 566,
        "sentence_index": 33,
        "raw": "These forms are the same as those noted above for Kōlāmī .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 566,
        "sentence_index": 35,
        "raw": "The past tense is the same as in Kōlāmī .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 566,
        "sentence_index": 39,
        "raw": "BHĪLĪ OF BASIM .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 567,
        "sentence_index": 6,
        "raw": "In most of the preceding characteristics and in other important points the Bhīlī of Basim agrees with Kōlāmī , as will be seen from the version of the Parable of the Prodigal Son which follows .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 622,
        "sentence_index": 45,
        "raw": "The dative and the accusative have the same form , as is also the case in some dialects of Tamil such as Kaikāḍī and Burgaṇḍī , and in Gōṇḍī , Naikī , and Kōlāmī .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 623,
        "sentence_index": 13,
        "raw": "The genitive suffix nā , ā , corresponds to Burgaṇḍī e , ne ; Naikī and Kōlāmī nē ; Gōṇḍī ā ; Kui i , ni , etc.",
        "disposition": "explicit_lexical_witness_separately_keyed",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 626,
        "sentence_index": 21,
        "raw": "A similar state of affairs is also found in Kōlāmī , Naikī , Kuī , and other dialects .",
        "disposition": "explicit_lexical_witness_separately_keyed",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 626,
        "sentence_index": 26,
        "raw": "The negative particle tōten in Kōlāmī is perhaps also a past tense of a negative verb , and in some Gōṇḍī dialects an inflected hille is used .",
        "disposition": "explicit_lexical_witness_separately_keyed",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 627,
        "sentence_index": 6,
        "raw": "The t-forms can perhaps be compared with Kōlāmī tōten , and similar forms appear to be current in Tuḷu where we find maḷpuji , I do not wake ; maḷt ’ diji , I did not wake , etc.",
        "disposition": "explicit_lexical_witness_separately_keyed",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 473,
        "sentence_index": 10,
        "raw": "Gōṇḍ communities speak the language in Akola , in the centre of Basim , and , partly interspersed with Kōlāms , in the district of Wun .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 474,
        "sentence_index": 2,
        "raw": "Kōlāmī and Naikī , on the other hand , which have hitherto been considered as dialects of Gōṇḍī , differ so much that they must be separated as a different language .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 478,
        "sentence_index": 68,
        "raw": "Haig , Captain Wolseley , A Comparative Vocabulary of the Gōṇḍī and Kōlāmī Languages .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 478,
        "sentence_index": 79,
        "raw": "Thus we find hōr , that , in Raipur , Khairagarh , Bhandara , Nagpur , Wun , and Akola .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 480,
        "sentence_index": 28,
        "raw": "Similar forms are also found in Kaikāḍī and Kōlāmī .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 561,
        "sentence_index": 1,
        "raw": "KŌLĀMĪ , NAIKĪ , ETC .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 561,
        "sentence_index": 4,
        "raw": "The dialects in question are the so-called Kōlāmī , the Bhīlī spoken in the Pusad Taluqa of Basim , and the so-called Naikī of Chanda .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 561,
        "sentence_index": 8,
        "raw": "KŌLĀMĪ .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 561,
        "sentence_index": 9,
        "raw": "The Kōlāms are an aboriginal tribe in East Berar and the Wardha district of the Central Provinces .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 561,
        "sentence_index": 13,
        "raw": "Local estimates give 17,000 as the number of speakers in Wun .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 561,
        "sentence_index": 14,
        "raw": "At the last Census of 1901 , however , Kōlāmī was not returned from the district , and the number of Kōlāms was only 264 .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 561,
        "sentence_index": 16,
        "raw": "The number of speakers has been estimated for the purposes of this Survey as followš – A few speakers are probably also found in Pusad , in the Basim district .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 561,
        "sentence_index": 17,
        "raw": "The socalled Bhīlī of that district is , at all events , almost identical with Kōlāmī .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 561,
        "sentence_index": 19,
        "raw": "In the last Census of 1901 Kōlāmī was only returned from Wardha with a total of 1,505 speakers .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 561,
        "sentence_index": 20,
        "raw": "The Kōlāms are usually classed as a Gōṇḍ tribe .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 561,
        "sentence_index": 21,
        "raw": "According to Captain Haig , however , they ‘ differ considerably from Gōṇḍs in appearance , and the Gōṇḍs , in Berar , at any rate , do not admit that they are a Gōṇḍ tribe , while the Kōlāms on the other hand shew no anxiety to be considered so , but are rather inclined to repudiate the connection ’ .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 561,
        "sentence_index": 22,
        "raw": "The Kōlāmī dialect differs widely from the language of the neighbouring Gōṇḍṣ In some points it agrees with Telugu , in other characteristics with Kanarese and connected forms of speech .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 561,
        "sentence_index": 23,
        "raw": "There are also some interesting points of analogy with the Toda dialect of the Nilgiris , and the Kōlāms must , from a philological point of view , be considered as the remnants of an old Dravidian tribe who have not been involved in the development of the principal Dravidian languages , or of a tribe who have not originally spoken a Dravidian form of speech .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 562,
        "sentence_index": 8,
        "raw": "Haig , Captain Wolseley , A Comparative Vocabulary of the Gōṇḍi and Kōlāmī Languages .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 562,
        "sentence_index": 12,
        "raw": "The notes on Kōlāmī grammar which follow are based on the version of the Parable of the Prodigal Son printed below .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 562,
        "sentence_index": 21,
        "raw": "The feminine and neuter singular take the same form in Naikī , and this is probably also the case in Kōlāmī .",
        "disposition": "chapter_owner_scope",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 570,
        "sentence_index": 10,
        "raw": "In the Central Provinces and Berar it is usually stated to be a synonym of Banjārī , and in the Bombay Presidency it connotes a Bhīl dialect .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 570,
        "sentence_index": 13,
        "raw": "They show that the dialect in many important points agrees with Kōlāmī and differs from ordinary Gōṇḍī .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 570,
        "sentence_index": 29,
        "raw": "The same forms are usual in Kōlāmī .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 571,
        "sentence_index": 4,
        "raw": "Compare Kōlāmī .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 571,
        "sentence_index": 11,
        "raw": "Compare Kōlāmī .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 571,
        "sentence_index": 16,
        "raw": "Compare Kōlāmī .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 577,
        "sentence_index": 6,
        "raw": "It follows that river to its confluence with the Godavari , and then runs through Chanda , cutting off the southern part of that district , and farther eastwards , including the southern border of the district of Wun .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 283,
        "sentence_index": 33,
        "raw": "Some dialects such as Kōlāmī and Naikī have usually been considered as forms of Gōṇḍī , but will in this Survey be separated from that form of speech .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 284,
        "sentence_index": 27,
        "raw": "Some minor dialects such as Kōlāmī , Naikī , and the Bhīlī spoken in the Pusad Taluqa of Basim , should be classed in a similar way .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 290,
        "sentence_index": 6,
        "raw": "Most other languages of the family , Kurukh , Malto , Kui , Gōṇḍī , Kōlāmī , and Telugu , have no feminine singular but use the neuter instead .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 185,
        "sentence_index": 9,
        "raw": "Nahālī is different from the Nāhari dialect of Kanker , which is a broken Halabī , and also from Naharī , a Bhīl dialect of Nasik and Sargana .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 185,
        "sentence_index": 14,
        "raw": "To the north and west we find a continuous chain of dialects , viż , the various Bhīl dialects , which are now Aryan but are spoken by tribes who must have been of the same stock as the Nahālṣ A version of the Parable of the Prodigal Son and a list of Standard Words and Phrases in Nahālī have been received from Nimar and will be reproduced below .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 186,
        "sentence_index": 35,
        "raw": "Compare the common n suffix in Bhīlī and Khāndēśī .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 8,
        "sentence_index": 24,
        "raw": "The Nishādas are identified with the Bhillas .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 9,
        "sentence_index": 12,
        "raw": "The numerous Bhīl tribes occupy a territory of the same kind as that inhabited by the Muṇḍāṣ Their various dialects show some traces of Dravidian influence , and it seems allowable to infer that these are the result of the same development the first stage of which lies before us in Nahālī .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 167,
        "sentence_index": 16,
        "raw": "It is different from Nāharī , a broken form of Halabī spoken in the Kanker State , and from Naharī , a Bhīl dialect spoken in Nasīk and Sargana .",
        "disposition": "documentary_or_non_target_control",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      },
      {
        "printed_page": 182,
        "sentence_index": 36,
        "raw": "Compare Kōlāmī tōlen , and todī in the Dravidian Bhīlī of Berar .",
        "disposition": "explicit_lexical_witness_separately_keyed",
        "physical_literal_accounting_separate": true
      }
    ]
  },
